# Web Crawling

This module discovers Android projects on F-Droid and collects their GitHub issues for NCF bug-report mining.

## Files

- `crawling_repo_url.ipynb`: extracts GitHub repository URLs from F-Droid metadata.
- `fdroid_github_only.csv`: 2,941 unique GitHub repositories discovered by the crawler.
- `crawling_issues.ipynb`: downloads repository issues through the GitHub API and excludes pull requests.
- `newest_100_issues.json`: a small sample of the collected issue format.

The complete crawl contains 518,027 issues. Download `all_issues_new.zip` from the [FineDroid Project Data folder](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Gcd3DOvtz2brau-ETGziX9KAn1119fgM?usp=sharing).

## Running the notebooks

Run `crawling_repo_url.ipynb` first, followed by `crawling_issues.ipynb`. Configure a GitHub token through the environment to avoid the unauthenticated API rate limit:

```bash
export GITHUB_TOKEN="xxx"
```

The main Python dependencies are `requests` and `beautifulsoup4`. The resulting issue files are consumed by the [NCF bug-report filtering module](../NCF_bug_report_filtering/readme.md).
